","comment":{"body":"<img width=\"1128\" height=\"452\" alt=\"test-output\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b008a80a-b01b-4d46-937b-df92dd753122\" />\r\n"}}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T13:47:04Z","repo":{"name":"kestra-io/kestra"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T12:24:47Z","repo":{"name":"collective/icalendar"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T11:30:59Z","repo":{"name":"kestra-io/kestra"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"<img width=\"1164\" height=\"452\" alt=\"test-output\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9206f7ee-0063-4b0d-9ed2-c6dd5ea70118\" />\r\n"}}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T11:28:01Z","repo":{"name":"kestra-io/kestra"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T09:39:28Z","repo":{"name":"google-gemini/gemini-cli"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T09:33:55Z","repo":{"name":"Ericsson/codechecker"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T08:55:12Z","repo":{"name":"google-gemini/gemini-cli"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T08:48:31Z","repo":{"name":"google-gemini/gemini-cli"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Closing in favor of #29606 — same change, but the commit in that PR is authored with the GitHub noreply address so the cla/google check can match the CLA (this PR's commit author email could not be attributed). No review was started here, so nothing is lost."}}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T08:48:21Z","repo":{"name":"google-gemini/gemini-cli"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T08:42:20Z","repo":{"name":"google-gemini/gemini-cli"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"The Google Individual CLA now lists the GitHub username `author` (updated on cla.developers.google.com just now). Could you please re-run the cla/google check? Thank you!"}}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T07:20:44Z","repo":{"name":"BytePioneer-AI/codex-host"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T05:37:36Z","repo":{"name":"google-gemini/gemini-cli"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T14:45:34Z","repo":{"name":"openai/codex"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Confirmed that this still occurs with the current macOS desktop build:\n\n- Codex App: `26.928.21956`\n- Bundled Codex CLI: `0.159.2`\n- macOS: `27.0.1`, Apple Silicon (`Darwin 27.0.0 arm64 arm`)\n\nThe desktop log reports the following immediately after selecting Uninstall for a personal skill. The username and custom skill name are redacted:\n\n```text\n2026-10-01T14:19:57.331Z warning [electron-fetch-handler] Failed to remove skill error=\"Skill path is not removable: /Users/<user>/.agents/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md\"\n```\n\nThe same error was also recorded on September 24. The affected skill is a real directory, not a symlink; it and its parent directories are owned by the current user, writable, and have no immutable flags.\n\n### Additional diagnosis\n\nThe installed desktop app's removal-path check accepts a skill directory under the Codex home `skills` root, or a descendant of a `.codex/skills` directory, but does not accept the supported discovery root `~/.agents/skills`.\n\nI evaluated only the path-validation helper, without invoking the filesystem removal operation:\n\n| Skill directory | Accepted by the removal-path check |\n| --- | --- |\n| `~/.agents/skills/<skill>` | No |\n| `~/.codex/skills/<skill>` | Yes |\n\nThis rejection happens before filesystem deletion. It is not a skill-sync tool restoring the files after a successful uninstall. The failing skill was not registered with the local third-party skill manager.\n\nDuplicate copies can make the workaround confusing: removing a copy from one discovery root may expose another copy with the same skill name in the other root. Those sources should not be silently conflated.\n\n### Proposed fix\n\n1. **Use one source-root policy for discovery, installation, and removal.** Resolve the effective Codex home and the current user's actual home directory, and include the supported user-level `~/.agents/skills` root in the removal allowlist. Prefer carrying the discovered source root and ownership/management metadata with the skill record rather than inferring ownership from a path substring.\n2. **Keep removal narrowly scoped.** Normalize the requested `SKILL.md` or skill-directory path, require a valid direct skill-directory child of an explicitly supported root, and never allow removal of the root itself, parent directories, traversal targets, or arbitrary directories merely because an ancestor is named `.agents/skills`.\n3. **Handle symlinks explicitly.** For a linked skill, remove only the installed link, not an external manager's source directory. For real directories, validate canonical root containment before recursive deletion. Define behavior for dangling links rather than treating them as generic missing skills.\n4. **Make shared-directory ownership visible.** Since `~/.agents/skills` can be read by other coding agents, show the source path and warn that removing a shared skill can affect them. If Codex intentionally does not manage that source, hide/disable Uninstall and explain how to remove it externally instead of offering an action that always fails.\n5. **Surface an actionable error and refresh discovery after success.** Do not reduce a deliberate source-policy rejection to a generic \"Failed to uninstall skill\" toast. If a same-name copy remains in another root, identify that source instead of implying that the original deletion failed.\n\n### Suggested regression coverage\n\n- A real `~/.agents/skills/test-skill` directory can be removed when it is a managed source; its root and sibling skills remain intact.\n- Existing `~/.codex/skills` behavior and a custom `CODEX_HOME/skills` root continue to work.\n- Passing either the discovered `SKILL.md` path or the supported skill-directory path yields the same result.\n- Relative traversal, the skills root itself, similarly prefixed sibling roots, and arbitrary out-of-root targets are rejected.\n- An installed symlink is unlinked without deleting its external target; dangling links have explicit behavior.\n- Same-name skills in two roots remain separate removal targets.\n- Filesystem permission errors retain their actual cause.\n- Intentionally unmanaged/shared sources do not display an enabled but unusable Uninstall action.\n\nNo application bundle was modified as part of this diagnosis.\n"}}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T14:40:00Z","repo":{"name":"BytePioneer-AI/codex-host"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T14:21:22Z","repo":{"name":"VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaMetrics"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T12:33:12Z","repo":{"name":"farion1231/cc-switch"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"此需求已有功能 PR **#7157**：https://github.com/farion1231/cc-switch/pull/7157，包含 Codex 下的 GitHub Copilot 托管账号选择及能力驱动 Responses/Chat 路由，作者为 @ljie-PI。当前尚未合并，不应把它当作已发布功能。\n\n我采用“复用并补齐”，没有再开重复需求 issue 或整包功能 PR。对其固定 head `0b49369056bed6038615e990efd272b2987ebcc1` 做了本地验证，并向原作者的功能分支提交 **tests-only** 补强 PR：https://github.com/ljie-PI/cc-switch/pull/1。\n\n新增 7 项回归覆盖已有卡片非默认/旧账号绑定的编辑保存、managed/legacy 优先级、pending/error 与缺失绑定时的表单提交保护；不宣称修复了新运行时缺陷。\n\n结果：补丁后前端目标 **82/82**、完整前端 **1,753/1,753**，typecheck/格式/build 通过；原功能 Copilot Rust 测试 **160/160**、cargo check/fmt 通过。完整 Rust 在跳过一个被本地运行应用占用固定端口的现有测试后 **3,207 通过、9 ignored、1 filtered**。严格 Clippy 在本机 Rust 1.98 下有 4 个现有诊断，仓库指定的 1.95 未测，因此不是“所有检查全部通过”。详细边界与命令见补丁 PR 及官方讨论：https://github.com/farion1231/cc-switch/pull/7157#issuecomment-5931491283。\n\n未使用真实 Copilot 账号/云端请求/额度，也未替换安装应用；认证全链路和真实云端兼容性仍未验证。后续是否合并与发布由维护者决定。"}}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T13:57:32Z","repo":{"name":"redis/redis"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T11:14:24Z","repo":{"name":"ARPAHLS/skillware"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Following up on this issue through #334 and taking responsibility for its remaining review items. The missing documentation for the shared version/install-conflict advisory opt-out is now addressed in a548689. This follow-up is AI-assisted.\n"}}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T12:44:22Z","repo":{"name":"prettier/prettier"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T12:33:10Z","repo":{"name":"farion1231/cc-switch"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"补丁已提交到原功能分支：**https://github.com/ljie-PI/cc-switch/pull/1**，提交 `4a0272ae`（https://github.com/author/cc-switch/commit/4a0272ae）。\n\n只有一个测试文件、7 个新增回归用例，没有重复提交功能实现，也没有改生产代码。补丁后 Copilot/Codex 前端目标测试 **82/82**；完整前端 **1,753/1,753**。Rust 跳过本地被占用固定端口的一个无关测试后 **3,207 通过、9 ignored、1 filtered**；Clippy/toolchain 与真账号未测边界已写在补丁 PR。\n\n如这些测试适合此 PR，可合并 companion PR 或 cherry-pick 上述提交。感谢原实现与维护工作。"}}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T12:32:40Z","repo":{"name":"ljie-PI/cc-switch"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T12:29:58Z","repo":{"name":"farion1231/cc-switch"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"我在需求 #6700 的基础上验证了此 PR，采用“复用并补齐”而不是重复实现。感谢 @ljie-PI 的功能实现。\n\n固定验证 head：`0b49369056bed6038615e990efd272b2987ebcc1`。目前没有确认需要修改生产代码的新运行时缺陷，但现有表单测试没有直接覆盖“编辑已有 Copilot 卡片”的非默认/旧账号绑定保存链路。我补了一个 **tests-only** companion patch（7 个用例，仅改 `ProviderForm.codexCopilot.test.tsx`），准备向此 PR 的原分支提交：\n\n- 非默认 managed account、旧 `githubAccountId` 的编辑→保存；\n- managed `authBinding` 优先于冲突 legacy 字段，显式默认绑定不被旧字段覆盖；\n- 账号状态 pending/error 时阻止保存，表单仍持有不存在的绑定 ID 时拒绝提交；\n- 这些 round-trip 用例同时检查空 `auth`、Responses 客户端 wire protocol 与保存的上游协议。\n\n本地结果（macOS arm64，Node 22.23.2 / pnpm 10.12.3 / Homebrew Rust 1.98）：\n- 原 PR 前端目标测试 75/75；补丁后全量 Vitest `--maxWorkers=2 --minWorkers=1` 1,753/1,753（151 个文件）；typecheck、src 格式、修改测试格式和 renderer build 通过。\n- 原 PR Copilot Rust 测试 160/160；`cargo check --locked`、`cargo fmt --check` 通过。\n- 未过滤的 Rust 全套先在一个 Claude Desktop 测试失败：固定端口 15721 被本地已安装 CC Switch 占用。没有关闭应用；只跳过该测试后 3,207 项通过、9 项原有 ignored、1 项 filtered（详见后续补丁 PR）。\n- 首次前端全套在同时编译 Rust 时有一个现有 PiProviderForm 用例 5 秒超时；未修改该用例，降低 worker 数后全套通过。\n- 严格 Clippy 在本机 1.98 报 4 个现有生产代码诊断；仓库指定 1.95，本次未验证指定 toolchain 的 Clippy，不将其写为通过。\n\n**边界**：没有使用真实 Copilot 账号、云端请求或订阅额度；后端设 `CC_SWITCH_TEST_HOME` 隔离。新增测试刻意 mock 账号选择组件，只验证表单加载/提交，不声称验证真实 widget 自动解绑、完整 token 刷新或 Copilot HTTP 端到端。两次临时 resolver mutation（丢失 managed ID / 错让旧 ID 优先）均被新 round-trip 用例检测到，生产文件已恢复。\n"}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T12:16:22Z","repo":{"name":"openssl/openssl"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"For head 3918ac8, the [Windows ARM64 job](https://github.com/openssl/openssl/actions/runs/36853049615/job/110339025888) reports a missing path when calling `vcvarsarm64.bat`, then cannot find `cl`; the [GnuTLS job](https://github.com/openssl/openssl/actions/runs/36853068361/job/110339071105) reports a certificate-setup extension error for `HOME=.` and subsequently missing `ca/cert.pem`.\n\nThis PR changes only `INSTALL.md` and `NOTES-PERL.md`; could a maintainer advise whether these failures need a CI setup fix or a rerun, while the remaining checks finish?\n\nAI-assisted diagnostic, posted on behalf of the PR author.\n"}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T12:15:27Z","repo":{"name":"dotnet/runtime"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"For head d45ebc7, the failing SuperPMI tpdiff run has two concrete tooling errors: the [windows-x64-2 Helix log](https://helix.dot.net/api/2019-06-17/jobs/2c8671c7-ff31-4c65-a41d-44805af78ad2/workitems/windows-x64-2/console) reports Intel Pin `PrepareToAttach(): Current thread holds VM lock`, followed by a missing `*_details.csv`; the [summary step](https://dev.azure.com/dnceng-public/public/_apis/build/builds/1618189/logs/178) fails in `superpmi.py` with `ValueError: too many values to unpack (expected 5)`.\n\nCould a maintainer advise whether these match a known build error and what the appropriate next step is? These logs alone do not establish whether the PR caused the failure.\n\nAI-generated diagnostic, posted on behalf of the PR author.\n"}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T11:14:30Z","repo":{"name":"ARPAHLS/skillware"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Addressed the remaining documentation point in a548689: docs/usage/api_keys.md now explicitly says SKILLWARE_NO_VERSION_CHECK=1 suppresses both version and install-conflict advisories, with a changelog entry. The existing opt-out regression test is included in validation.\n\nLocal validation: 135 tests passed across test_version_policy.py, test_cli.py, test_registry_docs.py, and test_skill_docs.py; Black and Flake8 passed on the version-policy/CLI test paths; git diff --check passed. This was focused validation, not the complete optional-dependency suite. Hosted CI on the new head still needs to run.\n\nThe follow-up was AI-assisted. No implementation or package-version changes were made in this update.\n"}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T11:12:42Z","repo":{"name":"HIPS/autograd"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Fixed in 6169906. I reproduced the discrepancy: the example's old gradient was `[-0.80065654+0.39251418j, -0.12639565-0.01758187j]`; it is now `[0.88941665-0.06368912j, 0.11058335+0.06368912j]`, matching JAX with x64 enabled.\n\nThe complex case needs the conjugated phase in the log-magnitude derivative. Its forward tangent must also be real. I added the phase-output derivative too, since complex sign is not piecewise constant: with `t = d(sum) / sum`, the output tangents are `real(t)` and `sign * (t - real(t))`.\n\nValidation:\n- New finite-difference checks cover the entire `(log-magnitude, phase)` tuple through second order in forward and reverse modes, complex and real inputs with complex weights, broadcast weights, multiple axes (including negative tuples), and both `keepdims` values\n- Separate comparison against JAX 0.11.2 with x64 enabled: log-magnitude values, JVPs and VJPs match in 28 cases\n- Full local suite: 649 passed\n- Repository-wide Ruff lint and format checks pass; `git diff --check` passes\n\nThe JAX comparison is specifically for log-magnitude: JAX currently gives zero derivatives for its complex sign output, so the phase derivative is checked against finite differences instead.\n"}}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T11:12:01Z","repo":{"name":"author/directus"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T11:09:21Z","repo":{"name":"composer/composer"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Updated in 8aa4db115. The website's heading generation does use different rules, including stripping the trailing root-only span.\n\nThe affected links now use explicit, unique anchors in the documents, while both renderers' generated heading anchors stay unchanged. This preserves existing website deep links and the table of contents.\n\nVerified all 23 affected links against GitHub's Markdown API and Parsedown 1.8.0 with the current getcomposer.org heading-generation code. All eight existing website anchors are still present, with no duplicate target IDs.\n"}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T10:25:11Z","repo":{"name":"dotnet/runtime"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"@dotnet-policy-service agree"}}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T09:33:09Z","repo":{"name":"chartjs/Chart.js"},"payload":